# Layout and Interaction Performance

- Read layout inputs through selectors and mutate them only through existing `layoutDispatch()` actions.
- Use `LayoutObserver`, device type, and current layout helpers; do not add competing viewport state or per-component resize systems.
- Coalesce geometry recalculation with existing throttle/debounce, `requestAnimationFrame`, and `layout-resize.ts` mechanisms.
- Keep interaction-only guards in refs or `Session` when they do not belong in rendered state.
- Publish layout, webcam-zone, presentation camera, or whiteboard state only when the computed value changed.
- Preserve `panZoomInterval`, wheel/pinch throttling, `zoomSlide` debounce, cursor interval, and existing subscription deduplication unless profiling proves a change is needed.
- Do not mix animated and instant camera updates without a user-interaction guard.
- Avoid broad DOM observers, repeated layout reads/writes, large state projections, and per-frame React state updates.
- Validate with no webcams, one webcam, many webcams, presentation, screenshare, mobile split zones, RTL, and panel open/close transitions.
- Assume large meetings and low-end mobile devices; prefer fewer renders, subscriptions, timers, and DOM nodes.
